Headless: the app's own map and a room search

THeadlessSession draws the 2D map only once a script opens one (openMapWidget(), Geyser.Mapper), and has no way to
find a room by name. An app on a phone shows the map whatever the scripts made, as the GUI's main window always
offers its mapper, and lets the player find a room on it. This adds a second TNullMapView the session owns, which
scripts do not hear of (no sysMapAreaChanged or sysMapWindowMousePressEvent from it): renderAppMap(),
appMapPointer(), showRoomOnAppMap() and closeAppMap(), and findRooms(), which matches room names as searchRoom()
does and the room id. setMapViewOnly() also switches while only the app's map is open.

Carried by Mudlet/android's scripts/apply-mudlet-patches.sh until Mudlet/Mudlet has it.

